  "rules": {
    "exact_offer_spec_claim_matrix_v1": "The frozen seller pages establish page assertions, not independently measured image quality. TCL SKU B095PGG2NB is 249.99 dollars with no posted review and describes a 64MP main camera in an AI-powered quad system. DJI SKU B08HWCCS6S is 499 dollars with no posted review and describes a 1/1.7-inch sensor, 64MP photos, 8x zoom and an AI Editor. Nikon SKU B07J2V97WQ is 6.24 dollars, rated 73 percent over twelve reviews, and describes a 16MP sensor, 40x optical zoom, 80x Dynamic Fine Zoom as enhanced digital zoom, and an included 64GB card. VJIANGER SKU B09JGPRCY5 is 119.99 dollars, rated 72 percent over ten reviews, and claims 48MP and 16x digital zoom. Panasonic SKU B0774KTV1X is 997.99 dollars with no posted review, body only selected, and says its 20.3MP sensor is shot eight times to create one 80MP RAW image in a special mode. KUIDAMOS SKU B093RDC7P7 is 73.69 dollars with no posted review and describes front and rear 2400W (720P) lenses, 200 DPI printing and AI-labelled automatic functions. The captured pages do not supply a matched resolved-detail, zoom, low-light or print trial.",
    "pixel_count_resolution_sampling_boundary_v1": "A pixel page describes pixels as samples and notes that camera-sensor terminology may refer to photosites or sensels. The image-resolution page calls image resolution the level of detail, distinguishes total, recorded and effective pixels, and says pixel-count resolutions are upper bounds rather than true resolution. The optical-resolution page defines resolved detail by scale and says lenses, recording components, environment, contrast, alignment, lens quality and diffraction affect real resolution. Pixel binning combines adjacent samples and can reduce noise or improve low-light output while lowering output resolution. Therefore 64MP, 48MP, 20.3MP, 80MP, 2400W, 720P and print DPI cannot be ranked as one physical detail scale without exact definitions, files, optics and measurements, and 64GB remains storage capacity.",
    "optical_digital_zoom_physical_boundary_v1": "A zoom lens varies focal length and angle of view, and a zoom ratio is longest focal length divided by shortest focal length. Larger ranges can bring optical and operational compromises, and phone optical-zoom marketing may describe several fixed cameras combined with digital processing. Digital zoom crops and scales without adjusting the optics and adds no optical resolution. The Nikon page explicitly separates 40x optical zoom from 80x enhanced digital zoom. The VJIANGER page calls 16x digital zoom. The DJI page says 8x zoom but the captured text does not call it optical. A valid comparison therefore needs exact wide and telephoto endpoints or equivalents, aperture, support and stabilization, target distance, field of view, optical-only files and matched crop baselines rather than ranking the largest multiplier.",
    "computation_reconstruction_ai_scope_boundary_v1": "A Bayer sensor records one filtered color at each site and demosaicing estimates the missing color components; algorithms can produce varying quality, false color, lost detail and edge artifacts. Binning combines samples and may use self-claimed AI while reducing output resolution. Computational photography uses digital computation instead of or alongside optical processes. Super-resolution can improve an output through multiple exposures or inference but remains limited by physics and information and may require scene invariance. These concepts do not validate a seller's exact product. DJI's captured AI Editor combines video clips with transitions and music, not measured still-image detail. TCL's AI-powered camera and precise-detail language and KUIDAMOS's AI-labelled autofocus, color or discoloration and dimming remain unspecified seller claims until mode, input, output, operation and matched effect are verified. Panasonic's eight-shot 80MP mode must be tested as a multi-exposure output path, not relabelled as a native sensor.",
    "current_identity_file_metadata_gate_v1": "Before testing, verify the physical product and selected configuration, seller and manufacturer, model and serial identity, lens or camera module, firmware and app version, manual, current primary specification, capture mode, digital-zoom setting, stabilization, output dimensions, file type, EXIF or equivalent metadata, RAW or JPEG path, included storage and delivered total system cost. Obtain sample files rather than relying on titles. Unresolved 2400W units, unlabeled DJI zoom type, missing focal-length endpoints, unavailable mode definitions or mismatched files block that claim-level verdict instead of inviting a conversion or guess.",
    "matched_scene_print_zoom_trial_v1": "After identity and metadata gates pass, use a fixed high-detail chart plus representative daylight, dim indoor and distant scenes. Match viewpoint, target distance, illumination, exposure policy, support, field of view or declared framing, focus verification and final display or print conditions. Preserve native files. Compare optical endpoints with same-position crops, disable digital zoom for the optical baseline, and test digital, binning, multi-shot, super-resolution or other computational modes as separate factors. Predeclare thresholds for resolved line pairs or target detail, noise, false detail, halos, color artifacts, motion blur, multi-shot ghosting, output dimensions, print size, processing time and failure rate. Results remain local to the tested unit, firmware, mode, scene, support and output.",
    "evidence_bounded_camera_spec_choice_v1": "The packet cannot establish that the largest megapixel number, 40x or 80x multiplier, or any AI label is the best camera. Preserve exact seller assertions, resolve units and current identity, separate sensor sampling from recorded output and resolved detail, separate optical focal-length change from crop enlargement, identify every computational operation, and run the matched file and print trial. Choose the lowest delivered total system cost exact path that clears the declared daylight, dim-scene, distant-subject, detail, artifact, motion, output and workflow thresholds. If no single path clears all gates, keep separately validated paths for different uses or defer. Do not issue a universal brand, sensor-size, megapixel, zoom or AI-quality verdict."
